Error [jet.TypestateMarkerRetired]: `#State` markers on `Door` are retired
  --> tests/ui/typestate/state_section_shape_diagnostics_are_distinct_5.jet:4:5
    |
  4 |     #State(Ready) open: fn(self) {}
    |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: State types carry these facts: a parameter typed `Owner.A` requires `A`, a result typed `Owner.B` moves the value to `B`, and the owner's state list names each move as `A -> B`
 Fix: Write the states into the signature (`self: &&Door.A`, `-> Door.B`), add `A -> B` to the state list of `Door`, and delete the marker
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0175
